People and processes are time-dependent particle sources (@cm-personnel-source: 0, is #chapter, #part-of @clean-manufacturing, #source "../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X", #source "../sources/Demand-Controlled-Cleanroom-Filtration-Faulkner-Fisk-Walton.lingua#r_2W1ADE030W9RFA8ATDKSYVT6XP", #source "../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X", #clean-manufacturing "Garments-and-handling-change-transfer-paths.lingua#r_62FB747EWEP7AJEH02XYA39W34") { r_5PR0C1S8SCP2HH8XMTSWNBW0RY
**Read:** [Cleanroom programming and energy — Tschudi, Sartor and Xu](../sources/Cleanroom-Programming-and-Energy-LBNL.lingua#r_36R5RS6HEWBTYN4SHCVPQNP12X), process and occupancy; [Demand-controlled cleanroom filtration — Faulkner, Fisk and Walton](../sources/Demand-Controlled-Cleanroom-Filtration-Faulkner-Fisk-Walton.lingua#r_2W1ADE030W9RFA8ATDKSYVT6XP), observed occupancy and concentration; [Air-cleaning systems — DOE-HDBK-1169-2022](../sources/Air-Cleaning-Handbook-DOE.lingua#r_09QPEZ76E9W6HS7R55X2K8TB3X), contaminant origins.

Motion, abrasion, clothing, handling and equipment release material at different rates and locations. Represent a source as G(t), with a defined size or chemical class and units, rather than assigning every person an invariant particle count.

One averaged emission rate can hide a brief release near a critical surface. Occupancy counts do not uniquely determine activity, garment state, tools or airflow obstruction. Airborne number, viable recovery and deposited material remain different observations.

**Work:** Propose an observation sequence distinguishing background, one handling task and one equipment cycle. Keep the actual measurement interval and uncertainty. Build a hypothetical source history and compare equal total releases delivered steadily or as a short pulse; follow both through the later room balance.

**Return:** [Clean manufacturing and contamination control — from familiar objects to controlled processes](../Clean-manufacturing-and-contamination-control.lingua#r_7D8SQ8BVQDZQBDBGC6DP0JAMZN).
